The \emph{wrapped length}
\begin{equation} \abs{w}_{G \cup D} \coloneqq \min \set*{\, k : w = g_1 \cdots g_k,\ g_j \in G \cup D \,}
\end{equation}
is the minimum number of symbols from $G \cup D$ in any factorization of $w$, and the
\emph{raw} (unwrapped) length $\abs{w}_G$ uses $G$ alone.

